I have read _An Enemy of the State_ (someone, possibly Karl Sackett,
had put a WSPQ card in the library's copy, which I dutifully left in).

The book pits a dictator and his ministers of state against a
Robin-hoodish outlaw, letting us see what goes on in both camps. The
outlaw wages a propaganda and terrorist war against the federation,
and shows in considerable detail how the economy grinds itself into
filings and overheats under the dictator's heavy-handed attempts to
control it while continuing to debase the currency and increase the
government's budget. The outlaw conspiracy works to set up a free
hard-money economy.

The economics parallel and parody the dynamics of wage and price
controls under Nixon and Ford in particular, but generalize OK.

It's a very entertaining and very subversive read.

BTW, Neal Stephenson's _Snow Crash_ is now out in paperback for
$5.99. It's not Libfic, but most people of Extropian bent will
enjoy the VR and the playful use of semantics. ESR will like it
because it weaves magic and computer science together ;-).
